;; products.edn -- the commercial go-to-market catalog for
;; cloud-itonami-hygiene-access. Four representative SKUs spanning both
;; active ingredients and all three product types. Loosely mirrors
;; `etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-yakushi`'s own `products.edn` `:product/*`
;; vocabulary (`:product/id` `:product/title` `:product/price-minor`
;; `:product/currency`) where it transfers, extended with this actor's
;; own commercial fields under the `:hygaccess.product/*` namespace
;; (formulation / packaging / target-market / claim / channel).
;;
;; INTERNAL CONSISTENCY: every SKU's declared
;; `:hygaccess.product/concentration-pct` falls within
;; `hygaccess.registry/efficacy-window-pct`'s own closed window for its
;; `[active product-type]` pair; every `:product/price-minor` falls at
;; or under `hygaccess.registry/price-ceiling-minor`'s own ceiling for
;; its product type; every `:hygaccess.product/packaging-format` is a
;; member of `hygaccess.registry/valid-packaging-formats`; every
;; `:hygaccess.product/claim` is a verbatim member of
;; `hygaccess.registry/substantiated-claims` for its product type; and
;; every `:hygaccess.product/channel` is a member of
;; `hygaccess.registry/valid-distribution-channels`. This file is
;; designed to pass the same governor logic `hygaccess.governor-
;; contract-test` exercises, conceptually -- it does not ship a
;; formulation/price/claim/format this actor's own checks would reject.
;;
;; TARGET MARKETS vs MARKET APPROVAL: `:hygaccess.product/target-
;; countries` below is a go-to-market ROADMAP (aspirational + already-
;; approved markets), not a claim that every listed country is already
;; independently approved in the store's `market-entry-approvals`
;; ground-truth table. Per the seeded sample data
;; (`hygaccess.store/sample-data!`), IN/BD/ID/PH/SA/AE are
;; `:approved? true`; PK/EG are `:approved? false` (pending local
;; regulatory review). A real `:propose-market-entry` proposal against
;; a pending country is correctly HARD-held by
;; `hygaccess.governor/market-not-approved-violations` until that
;; review completes -- this actor does not itself grant regulatory
;; market access (see README `What this actor does NOT do`).

